---
import SiteLayout from '../layouts/SiteLayout.astro';
import { content } from '../content/foundation';
import { catalog } from '../content/examples';
import { astroFlow } from '../content/astro-flow';
const sources = [...new Map([...content.sources, ...catalog.sources, ...astroFlow.sources].map((source) => [source.url, source])).values()];
---
<SiteLayout title="Sources and scope">
  <div class="page-intro"><a href="/">← Introduction</a><h1>Follow the reasoning.</h1><p>Tool rules, maintainer guidance and this guide’s own choices are different kinds of evidence.</p></div>
  <section class="scope-card" aria-labelledby="scope-heading"><h2 id="scope-heading">Original examples, visible limits.</h2><p>The trees, diagrams and explanations are original teaching illustrations. Linked templates and official examples remain separate references. Citation alone does not authorize copying; each example card includes a specific-use provenance record.</p><p>The opening map is one possible partial TypeScript project. It demonstrates responsibilities, not a runnable scaffold or universal directory rule. Folder names do not connect files automatically. Imports, configuration, test discovery and documentation conventions depend on the tools chosen.</p><p>These lessons are source-reviewed. The illustrated Go and Astro runtime experiments have not been executed. Tests of this website verify its interface and content contracts, not those language experiments. No learner study, real-device or screen-reader evaluation is claimed.</p><p>Selections stay in memory and reset when their page reloads. Only the Go layout guide exports a record; the landing story, catalog, Astro journey and naming lab are outside that export.</p></section>
  <section class="sources-section" id="sources" aria-labelledby="sources-heading"><div class="section-heading"><span class="step">THE RESEARCH TRAIL</span><h2 id="sources-heading">Claims you can follow.</h2><p>Each deeper explanation links the evidence for its particular claim. Mutable references may change after review.</p></div><div class="source-list">{sources.map((source) => <article><span class="eyebrow">{source.publisher}</span><h3><a href={source.url} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">{source.title} ↗<span class="sr-only"> (opens in a new tab)</span></a></h3><p>{source.section}</p><small>{source.version}<br />Checked {source.checkedAt} · Review after {source.reviewAfter}</small></article>)}</div></section>
  <section class="scope-card"><h2>Opening story and motion</h2><p>The introduction is independently authored, with a complete static map and one optional replay. It uses role highlighting rather than implying that a folder structure executes itself.</p><ul><li><a href="https://www.typescriptlang.org/docs/handbook/2/modules.html" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">TypeScript: modules<span class="sr-only"> (opens in a new tab)</span></a> explains explicit module connections, distinct from directory grouping.</li><li><a href="https://www.w3.org/WAI/WCAG22/Understanding/pause-stop-hide.html" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">W3C: Pause, Stop, Hide<span class="sr-only"> (opens in a new tab)</span></a> informs the pause control and complete reduced-motion alternative.</li></ul><p class="small muted">References checked 2026-10-14. No third-party code, diagram or prose is reproduced in the opening illustration.</p></section>
</SiteLayout>
